ted States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 5 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912810056},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n1. The census data has the 'United States' row with POPESTIMATE2025 = 341784857\n2. The farmers_markets table has state data\n\nNow I need to get the total farmers markets excluding territories. Let me check what the data looks like and which rows might be territories.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NB7nnH2MmAqLwxBq5SMmL6","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_name', 'state_abbr')","limit":0}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":209,"cacheRead":16857,"cacheWrite":841,"totalTokens":17921,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0010450000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0016857,"cacheWrite":0.00105125,"total":0.00379595},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":77},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912810056,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75F7de7gd7PfX4NVo4m","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01NB7nnH2MmAqLwxBq5SMmL6","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\"\n\"California\",\"CA\"\n\"New York\",\"NY\"\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\"\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\"\n\"Illinois\",\"IL\"\n\"Virginia\",\"VA\"\n\"Wisconsin\",\"WI\"\n\"Michigan\",\"MI\"\n\"Massachusetts\",\"MA\"\n\"Florida\",\"FL\"\n\"Georgia\",\"GA\"\n\"Ohio\",\"OH\"\n\"Texas\",\"TX\"\n\"Missouri\",\"MO\"\n\"North Carolina\",\"NC\"\n\"Iowa\",\"IA\"\n\"Kentucky\",\"KY\"\n\"Indiana\",\"IN\"\n\"Colorado\",\"CO\"\n\"Washington\",\"WA\"\n\"Maryland\",\"MD\"\n\"Connecticut\",\"CT\"\n\"Kansas\",\"KS\"\n\"Oregon\",\"OR\"\n\"Alabama\",\"AL\"\n\"Oklahoma\",\"OK\"\n\"Arizona\",\"AZ\"\n\"Tennessee\",\"TN\"\n\"South Carolina\",\"SC\"\n\"New Jersey\",\"NJ\"\n\"Montana\",\"MT\"\n\"Arkansas\",\"AR\"\n\"Louisiana\",\"LA\"\n\"Vermont\",\"VT\"\n\"Alaska\",\"AK\"\n\"Idaho\",\"ID\"\n\"West Virginia\",\"WV\"\n\"Wyoming\",\"WY\"\n\"Nebraska\",\"NE\"\n\"District Of Columbia\",\"DC\"\n\"New Hampshire\",\"NH\"\n\"Mississippi\",\"MS\"\n\"Delaware\",\"DE\"\n\"Maine\",\"ME\"\n\"New Mexico\",\"NM\"\n\"Rhode Island\",\"RI\"\n\"Utah\",\"UT\"\n\"Nevada\",\"NV\"\n\"North Dakota\",\"ND\"\n\"South Dakota\",\"SD\"\n\"Hawaii\",\"HI\"\n\"Puerto Rico\",\"PR\"\n\"Virgin Islands\",\"VI\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912813583},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see that the data includes territories like Puerto Rico (PR) and Virgin Islands (VI). The task asks for \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\". I need to determine which rows to exclude. \n\nThe U.S. territories typically include:\n- Puerto Rico (PR)\n- Virgin Islands (VI)\n- Guam (GU)\n- American Samoa (AS)\n- Northern Mariana Islands (MP)\n\nLooking at the data, I see PR and VI. Let me exclude these. I could also exclude territories based on a list of excluded state abbreviations.\n\nLet me create a build script that calculates the metric (farmers markets per 100,000 residents).","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01WZFNwS2D64DTU6BmzWSQNi","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_fm_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Read census data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Filter out territories from farmers markets data\n# US territories are: PR, VI, GU, AS, MP\nterritories = [\"PR\", \"VI\", \"GU\", \"AS\", \"MP\"]\nfm_us = fm.filter(~fm.state_abbr.isin(territories))\n\n# Calculate total farmers markets excluding territories\nfm_total = fm_us.aggregate(total_fm=fm_us.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_pop = census.filter(census.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025').mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(fm_per_100k=fm_total.total_fm / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select('total_fm', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'fm_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":775,"cacheRead":17698,"cacheWrite":592,"totalTokens":19078,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0038750000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0017698000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00074,"total":0.006397800000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":157},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912813583,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75FNa4TcsWw3YhRThF2","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01WZFNwS2D64DTU6BmzWSQNi","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1409 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_fm_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912821495},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll build this script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JE4yZ5wU8P4qgiEPG5RcUS","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-75-_dfa3196 && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_fm_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"cl